Confirmed the dead end. On a phone, autocapitalization makes the guard永远 false — the button never lights up, no request, no error, nothing happens. Exactly the report.

Now let me fix:

1. Three HTML inputs: add `autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"`.
2. Three JS guards: case-insensitive + accept bare name + live verdict text.

Let me look at the three JS guard sites precisely, plus see if there's a place to show the verdict. The modal HTML has:
```html
<div style="margin-bottom:12px">
  <label style="font-size:10px;color:var(--t2)">Введите имя репозитория для подтверждения:</label>
  <input ... id="delrepo-confirm" ...>
</div>
```
I'll add `<div id="delrepo-verdict" style="font-size:11px;margin-top:6px"></div>` after the input in each of the three HTML files, and update it from JS.

Let me write the shared guard logic per client:

```js
// The phone keyboard capitalises the first letter of every word, so what lands
// in the box is "Sj0404-collab/Zen-panel" and a case-sensitive compare never
// matched — the button stayed grey and nothing happened, with no error anywhere.
// GitHub names are case-insensitive anyway, so compare them that way and accept
// the bare repo name too.
const delrepoOk = v => {
  const t = String(v || '').trim().toLowerCase();
  return !!t && (t === fullName.toLowerCase() || t === fullName.split('/').pop().toLowerCase());
};
```

Then in the oninput handler update both the button and the verdict.

Let me write for each of the three files. I need the exact current code per file.

mobile-app.js:530-543:
```js
function ghDeleteRepoModal(fullName) {
  ghDeleteFullName = fullName;
  const info = document.getElementById('delrepo-info');
  if (info) info.textContent = 'Вы уверены, что хотите удалить ' + fullName + '?';
  const input = document.getElementById('delrepo-confirm');
  const btn = document.getElementById('delrepo-btn');
  if (input) { input.value = ''; input.oninput = function () { btn.disabled = this.value.trim() !== fullName; }; }
  if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Удалить навсегда'; }
  const bg = document.getElementById('modal-delrepo');
  if (bg) bg.classList.add('on');
  if (input) setTimeout(() => input.focus(), 50);
}
```

git-app.js:425-435 and desktop-app.js — let me read the desktop one.

To avoid triplicating logic, I could put the helper in `offline.js`... no, that's the offline layer. Better: each client gets a small shared-shaped helper. There are 3 files; duplication of 6 lines is acceptable and consistent with this codebase's style (the whole runner card is triplicated).

Let me read desktop-app.js's version.

